[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753107082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120406#issuecomment-4753107082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120406","id":4753107082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG06oig","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T16:00:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T16:04:49Z","body":"Can confirm, it is also reproducible in 4.7.dev1, haven't checked further.\nI don't think anything changed for SplitContainer that would have caused this, and the fact it only happens if you set it with the array index `split_containers[0].split_offsets[0] = offset` and not when assigning the entire array `split_containers[0].split_offsets = [ offset ]` makes me think it isn't caused by anything GUI, but instead by GDScript or somewhere else.\n\nI tested this on CPUParticles2D `emission_points`, and got the same result. In 4.6.2, `emission_points[0] = Vector2(5,5)` works but in 4.7.dev1 and 4.7 stable it doesn't.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4753107082/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875739981","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120406#issuecomment-4875739981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120406","id":4875739981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIp3jTQ","user":{"login":"Stavrolet","id":163565472,"node_id":"U_kgDOCb_PoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163565472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet","html_url":"https://github.com/Stavrolet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stavrolet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T11:38:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T11:41:53Z","body":"This probably isn't a bug, since it's specified in the documentation for all packed arrays. But for some reason, it still works in 4.6, even though the documentation says it shouldn't.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4875739981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4944326437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120406#issuecomment-4944326437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120406","id":4944326437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJrRvJQ","user":{"login":"nieboczek","id":106301320,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlYHiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106301320?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek","html_url":"https://github.com/nieboczek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nieboczek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T09:24:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T09:24:20Z","body":"The previous behavior was a bug, the documentation of the `split_offsets` property has a note informing that this shouldn't work. The code produces a warning in 4.7.stable. The same issue but with a different property, https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116375#issuecomment-3919522260 was closed as not planned.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4944326437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api